# A Vercel CLI deploy uploads the working copy from this directory. The CLI
# does not read .gitignore, and its built-in defaults drop only a few paths
# (.git, .vercel, node_modules, .env.local, .env.*.local and similar). So this
# file must exclude everything .gitignore excludes: otherwise a local .env,
# key file, Playwright session or agent note would ship in the deployment
# source. Git-integration builds start from the tracked tree, so leaving out
# untracked files can never remove a build input, and no rule here may match a
# tracked file. packages/website/src/lib/security/vercelignore.test.ts proves
# both: every untracked path .gitignore ignores is ignored here, and no tracked
# file is.

# Vercel installs dependencies and runs the build remotely, so neither the
# local dependency tree nor a local build output belongs in the upload. Without
# this file the CLI uploads ~782 MB (2.0 GB node_modules + 1.7 GB .next before
# compression) on every deploy, which is slow enough to time out.
node_modules
.next
packages/website/.next

# Local-only verification and test output. Playwright reports, traces and
# failure artifacts can hold cookies and screenshots of signed-in pages.
.lighthouseci
coverage
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
**/blob-report/

# Environment files. `next build` loads .env and .env.production from the app
# directory, so an uploaded file would reach the build as configuration. Hosted
# configuration comes only from the Vercel project's environment variables.
# The value-free .env*.example templates are tracked and stay uploadable.
**/.env*
!**/.env*.example
# The CLI already skips its project link, where `vercel pull` writes env files.
# Listed so this file stays a complete mirror of .gitignore.
.vercel

# Credentials and private keys.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa
**/id_dsa
**/id_ecdsa
**/id_ed25519
**/.npmrc
**/.netrc
**/.pypirc
**/.dockercfg
**/.git-credentials
**/.docker/config.json
**/.aws/
**/.kube/
**/.ssh/
**/kubeconfig
**/credentials.json
**/service-account*.json

# Session state: Playwright storage state can hold a real session token, and
# the Supabase CLI caches the linked project here.
**/tests/e2e/.auth/
**/supabase/.temp/

# Local agent instructions, agent tool state, scratch work and internal
# planning notes. They describe private workflows and can quote credentials or
# production details. Three .gitignore rules for internal note files are not
# repeated here: the publication scanner forbids naming those files in any
# tracked file except .gitignore, and the test derives that exception from the
# scanner's own rules.
**/CLAUDE.md
**/AGENTS.md
**/AGENT.md
**/INTEGRATION.md
**/.claude/
**/.claude-code/
**/.claude.json
**/.agents/
**/.cursor/
**/.cursorrules
**/.codex/
**/.gemini/
**/.windsurf/
**/.windsurfrules
**/.roo/
**/.roorules
**/.cline/
**/.continue/
**/.aider*
.github/copilot-instructions.md
**/scratchpad/
**/plans/
**/discuss-*.md
**/NOTES.md
**/*.local.md
docs/privacy/
docs/operations/
docs/launch-readiness.md
docs/open-source/github-org-release.md
docs/overhaul-*/

# Caches, other build output, other package managers' lockfiles, local-only
# test harnesses and editor litter. None is a build input.
.turbo/
.cache/
.bun-cache/
.firecrawl/
.swc/
.output/
dist/
build/
out/
*.log
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
.dev-ports.json
packages/website/tests/e2e/_*.spec.ts
**/bun.lock
!/bun.lock
**/bun.lockb
package-lock.json
npm-shrinkwrap.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~
.*.sw[a-p]
